{"kind":"request","text":"Hugh's authorized handoff: \"summarize these various improvements (we can discard the scope-combining option), assemble in approximate impact/priority order, and send them to planner in the workspace with a request to assess and implement according to their judgement.\"\n\nPlease assess the consolidated responsiveness opportunities below against current owned work, then commission and implement the worthwhile bounded slices according to your judgment. You own sequencing, scope, assignment and acceptance criteria. Reconcile with existing design, manifest/publication, settlement, query and provider owners; avoid duplicate tasks or competing gates. Return an assessment identifying selected work, ownership, measurements and any deferred/rejected options. This is authorization to assess and implement, not a claim that every candidate must be adopted. Physical combining of scope Durable Objects is discarded and out of this handoff.\n\nInvestigation basis: read-only main 38b0b2f2b, browser users and Cloudflare Artifacts host. Main at handoff f6d80b399 has no changes since that basis under packages/page/src, client/src, scope/src, git/src or platform/src. No benchmark or provider execution was performed. Counts below are source-derived, not measured wire latency; current Cloudflare APIs were checked against official documentation.\n\nApproximate impact/priority order (impact on routine responsiveness and scaling, tempered by effort/risk; adjust after measurement):\n\n1. SHORTEN THE BROWSER COMMAND RESPONSE PATH (M, moderate risk; immediate responsiveness).\nKeep the current subject visible and fence controls locally rather than initiating a whole pending redraw. Display the returned known action receipt immediately, independently of post-submit summary reads. Refresh only affected queries in the background; use authenticated head notifications so publication completion becomes visible without manual Check status/full reload. Deduplicate in-flight reads, cancel obsolete navigation reads, reuse verified immutable definitions and an explicit observed summary in declared-handle preparation.\nEvidence: packages/page/src/main.ts:218-249; data.ts:634-663; packages/client/src/declared.ts:196-205. Current generic lane submission has five serial HTTP requests (three summaries, POST, post-answer summary), plus overlapping pending/final full draws. Server streams already exist in scope/object.ts:242-254 and sessions.ts:453 onward; Page has no consumer.\nKeep returned answer, observation and downstream outcome distinct. Notifications trigger targeted authoritative reads, not settlement of an unidentified request. Retain exact command identity/recovery custody under existing settlement work; never replace an uncertain signed request.\n\n2. BOUNDED, HEAD-AWARE VIEW QUERIES AND LAZY INSPECTION (M initially / L for projections, moderate risk; removes room-size growth).\nRequest visible list kind/status/page; stop reading every issue and change lane sequentially. Provide publication/operation status scoped to the selected lane or merge, rather than scanning the whole destination history. Render primary subject first and load hidden inspection record families only when opened. Use bounded parallelism as an interim step, not client-only paging over full-room reads.\nEvidence: page/data.ts:261-280,387-423,428-441; main.ts:430. Warm list is about L+F+3 HTTP requests, where L includes all room lanes and F final-item pages; one-file change detail about14+C with one-page records and existing publication, where comment texts addC. Counts exclude renewal/eligibility/cache misses/retries.\nProjection is a non-authoritative query service with contributing scope heads, completeness/provenance and explicit unavailable/incomplete states. Do not invent one atomic room head or allow stale view data to decide mutations.\n\n3. ARTIFACTS-NATIVE SERVER READS (M-L, moderate/high integrity-boundary risk; eliminates credentials and Git-pack processing from ordinary reads).\nCurrent ArtifactsProvider.ref/format/objects/inspect each enters a fresh get/info/mint-read/Git-HTTP/revoke-read session. Site duplicates this. Introduce native binding reads where exact semantics match the existing integrity/servability checks; fallback to a bounded shared read session and verified object cache where raw Git semantics require smart HTTP. Preserve fresh mutable-ref observations separately from immutable content.\nEvidence: scope/artifacts-host.ts:186-216,240-252; site/host.ts:148-171; git/http-read.ts:419-450. Official binding already provides readCommit/readTree/readBlob/readFile/log: https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/api/workers-binding/ . Prove raw canonical commit/tree fidelity: metadata may normalize bytes, filenames/modes or headers. Avoid treating readFile alone as a replacement for publication verification.\nNative reads can also remove artifacts-wiring.ts:97-98's reason for excluding safe recovery: current reads mutate credentials. Assess this with recovery owner; do not silently change recovery semantics. Keep Git smart HTTP for ordinary clients and supported writes. Current Git transfer is binary, not a JSON/base64 relay.\n\n4. INCREMENTAL GIT PUBLICATION AND REUSE OF VERIFIED PREPARATION (L, high correctness risk; largest history/byte-amplification opportunity).\nOne-file judgment reads format/base closure and builds the edit; publication repeats those reads/builds, then supplies historical base closure plus new objects to the pack writer. Reuse verified immutable base objects/format/tree preparation; derive final commit at the recorded reservation time. Send changed blob, changed ancestor trees and new commit plus genuinely missing objects, with valid closure/host-possession evidence and restart reconstruction.\nEvidence: scope/destination-host.ts:288,321-328,389-406; artifacts-host.ts:194-206; git/reader.ts:283-305 (closure follows ancestor commits/trees/blobs); git/http.ts:98-145 (compresses all supplied objects). Under a single base-pack fetch assumption, one-file judge+write component paths use11 Git HTTP requests and7 read-token sessions, excluding write mint/revoke, receipt writes, coordination and retries.\nPreserve branch compare-and-swap, current credentials, exact expected tree/commit, own push answer, read-back and unknown-effect treatment. Do not blindly collapse separate post-push observations: sendOnce read-back and destination recorded seen have distinct duties.\n\n5. IMMUTABLE OBJECT AND RENDERED-PAGE CACHES / BACKGROUND PREPARATION (M-L, moderate risk; repeat reads and linked assets).\nCache verified object bytes by exact repository identity/object ID, and rendered representation by commit/path/renderer version and relevant frame inputs. Resolve HEAD independently. Prepare rendering/cache fills after durable publication; retain an on-demand fallback. Share/coalesce immutable reads so linked assets and concurrent reads do not repeat token setup, fetch/decompression and render.\nEvidence: git/http-read.ts:352,419-438; site/route.ts:305-355,367; site/host.ts:157-171. Worker-handled conditional requests perform ordinary read/servability work before304; an early cache hit requires a stated validity/access contract. Cache immutable bytes, not current authorization, revocation, mutable refs or redaction eligibility. Do not make site-token cleanup fire-and-forget; deferred cleanup needs durable custody/obligation, or eliminate read tokens with native reads.\n\n6. CONCURRENT INDEPENDENT DELIVERY, COALESCED WAKES AND POST-COMMIT NOTICES (M-L, moderate/high ordering risk; fan-out/tail latency).\nOutbox currently awaits every due duty before the next, including unrelated recipients. Introduce bounded concurrency across independent target scopes while preserving required recipient ordering/cycles. Durably mark attempts and persist earliest recovery wake before sending; assess one alarm update per safe batch instead of each duty. Coalesce or decouple operator indexing and stream fan-out from the authoritative commit section; these already cannot alter answers and operator catch-up is watermark-based.\nEvidence: scope/outbox.ts:128-170; operations.ts:385 already concurrently starts outside operations; object.ts:242-254; operator.ts:117-129. Creation involves four deliveries and four source-verification callbacks, excluding texts/definitions/authority. Source verification is essential provenance, not a dispensable relay.\nHappy-path dispatch already starts immediately at object.ts:217-222. One-second bounds are retry policies, not unavoidable per-event sleeps. Avoid adding a generic queue or extra relay to work that already dispatches durably. Measure Cloudflare output-gate behavior when moving post-commit storage work off the receipt path.\n\n7. ENCODE/PARSE ONCE AND REUSE INTERNALLY OWNED VERIFIED REPRESENTATIONS (S-M slices, moderate risk; lower priority until CPU/allocation profiling).\nEntry sealing canonicalizes for storage then entryHash canonicalizes again (scope/turn.ts:335-347, bytes/domains.ts:15,60). signedIntent captures canonical bytes, parses a detached intent, then re-canonicalizes for signing (client/intent.ts:92-101). Foreign entry bytes are parsed, verified, then canonicalized again for retention (scope/namespace.ts:184-195; core.ts:58-76).\nIntroduce an internally owned validated representation carrying value, exact canonical bytes, size and domain-separated digest; reuse bytes for hashing/storage/signing/retention and bounded parsed-entry caches. Preserve mutation isolation, strict input validation, exact domain tag+newline+canonical UTF-8, identical signatures/hashes and distrust of new ingress. RPC already exists between Worker and objects; there is no demonstrated second HTTP JSON layer to remove.\nAvoid a wire-codec migration or wholesale CBOR rewrite as first optimization. Likewise never remove defensive copies merely because they appear repetitive; several explicitly protect bytes across awaits. Indexed view responses in item2 remove more serialization than a faster codec over unnecessary history.\n\nSECONDARY INVESTIGATION, ONLY IF MEASUREMENTS JUSTIFY IT:\nBatch membership/authority observations from one head, preserving separately attributable subjects, required order/read numbering, freshness, revocation and second-phase dependencies. authority.ts:179-189 and core.ts:229-239 currently serialize subjects by explicit contract; destination judge can need rules, merger, holders and author observations. This requires authority/protocol assessment, not a Promise.all substitution. Measure object geography/placement; location hints are best-effort initial-creation behavior, not guaranteed co-location or relocation: https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/reference/data-location/ . Do not pursue scope combining.\n\nMEASUREMENT AND ACCEPTANCE:\nBefore ranking by wallclock, capture per-stage traces for browser acceptance, operation completion, visible update and Site read, with request/operation/fact IDs. Include cold/warm and increasing room/history sizes, p50/p95, request counts, transferred bytes, CPU/parse/compression work and unknown/restart outcomes. This is a suggested evidence set, not a command to run broad repeated suites.\nUse focused existing invariants at their cheapest boundaries; one coordinated final gate per complete review candidate per docs/testing.md, no mutation sweeps or competing/repeated whole suites. Validate both ordinary and lost-reply/restart paths for changed custody/delivery behavior.\nKeep synchronous prerequisites: authority/source verification, expected revision checks, due transitions before judgment, durable commit/attempt/recovery obligations, credential custody before external send, and publication confirmation before Merged. Only derived observation, independent work and safely recorded obligations may leave the response path.","body":{"conditions":"Assess the consolidated latency/transformation opportunities, reconcile existing ownership, and implement selected bounded work according to planner judgment. Return selection, sequencing, owners and semantic/measurement acceptance. Exclude combining scope Durable Objects.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}